In this project, I implemented a Binary Search Tree (BST) using C++.
* Created nodes dynamically to store data in the tree structure.
* Implemented insertion operations to add elements into the Binary Search Tree.
* Added searching functionality to find specific values in the tree.
* Implemented tree traversal methods including Preorder, Inorder, and Postorder.
* Found the minimum and maximum values present in the tree.
* Used recursive functions to perform tree operations efficiently.
* Implemented tree deletion to release dynamically allocated memory.
* Tested different BST operations to verify correct functionality.
This project helped me understand Binary Search Tree concepts, recursive programming, tree traversal techniques, dynamic memory management, and data structure implementation in C++.
